# ARK Companion: Communications

**Mission (frozen):** [docs/companion-v1/MISSION.md](../../docs/companion-v1/MISSION.md)

Internal product name: **ARK Companion: Communications** — advisor communications command center. Not ARKv2 mobile. Not legacy ARK Mobile tab refactor.

## Design philosophy

> **Every tap should reduce uncertainty for the advisor.**

Organizing question: *What does the advisor need to know before speaking?* — not *which screen should they open?*

Show what matters (posture, vehicle, last signal, ownership). Do not dump every authority field. ARK organizes around **advisor awareness** — not conversations alone (OpenPhone), CRM records (GHL), or repair orders (shop software).

## What to optimize for

Calls · texts · voicemails · conversations · customer/vehicle context · quick operational actions.

## UX benchmark

**OpenPhone / Quo** interaction quality — inbox density, thread navigation, swipe actions, live call UI, search, voicemail/recording playback, push-first workflow. Not a visual clone.

## ARK differentiation

Every conversation surfaces operational context inline: customer, vehicle, active RO, estimate/inspection status, parts pressure, advisor ownership, observations, AI summary (when earned).

> Communication comes first. Operations are available within communication.

## Deep-link boundary (sacred)

Answering a customer → Companion. Editing a repair order for two minutes → ARKv2.

Sustained work (RO editing, parts, production, reporting, scheduling) → **deep-link ARKv2**. Do not reproduce desktop workspaces in Companion. Litmus: more than a minute of operational editing → desktop.

## Build input (milestones only)

1. Inbox  
2. Conversation thread  
3. Calling  
4. Voicemail / recordings  
5. AI summary  
6. Context cards  
7. Push notifications  

Execute implementation from milestone + mission. **`screens/` specs are reference — not build order.**

## Authority lock

`/api/mobile/*` only. Sanctum. No parallel SMS inbox. No client-side estimate math. Voice: [ark-phone-mission.mdc](ark-phone-mission.mdc) · [ark-phone-production-telephony-lock.mdc](ark-phone-production-telephony-lock.mdc).

Communications doctrine: [communications-foundational-doctrine-v1.md](../../docs/communications/communications-foundational-doctrine-v1.md)

**Ownership freeze:** [ark-advisor-communications-identity.mdc](ark-advisor-communications-identity.mdc) — advisor-first; no new workstation/station automation during Companion.

## Anti-patterns

- Screen-by-screen implementation instructions when mission suffices
- Rebuilding RO workspace, workboard, or owner surfaces on mobile
- Generic CRM clone instead of Quo-grade comms rhythm + ARK operational context
- Patching legacy `lib/main.dart` module tabs — use `lib/companion/` entry
- Station/IP/browser ownership logic for comms — see [ark-advisor-communications-identity.mdc](ark-advisor-communications-identity.mdc)
